WEBVTT

00:01.500 --> 00:04.554
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.621 --> 00:07.975
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.026 --> 00:11.113
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:12.023 --> 00:14.928
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.995 --> 00:18.867
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.918 --> 00:21.721
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.805 --> 00:23.323
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.391 --> 00:24.759
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.844 --> 00:28.667
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.310 --> 00:39.081
(slurring): We interrupt this
program because I have had

00:39.148 --> 00:41.050
kind of a crap day,

00:41.118 --> 00:42.986
and I know all the station
passwords to do it.

00:43.054 --> 00:45.924
So, smell that finger, Quahog!

00:45.991 --> 00:48.294
Ooh, a drunk news report
from Tom Tucker.

00:48.361 --> 00:50.630
<i>We haven't had one of those
since they cancelled Passions.</i>

00:50.698 --> 00:52.133
This should be good.

00:52.201 --> 00:55.872
Okay, our top story tonight: a
local car dealer has announced

00:55.940 --> 00:59.177
a "Hands On A Hard Body"
promotion in which

00:59.245 --> 01:02.515
a used dirt bike will be rewar-
awarded to the one customer

01:02.583 --> 01:05.820
who can successfully outlast
his competitors.

01:05.888 --> 01:09.926
<i>And, and in other news, they're
bringing back Passions!</i>

01:09.994 --> 01:11.212
Yes, they are!

01:11.279 --> 01:12.713
Holy crap!
A dirt bike!

01:12.781 --> 01:13.765
That's awesome!

01:13.833 --> 01:15.735
Lois, I'm gonna win
that thing!

01:15.803 --> 01:17.638
Peter, why would you want
a used dirt bike

01:17.706 --> 01:19.341
when you already
have a car?

01:19.408 --> 01:21.277
Because this is 1978, Lois,

01:21.345 --> 01:22.778
and dirt bikes have
never been hotter.

01:22.846 --> 01:24.464
Besides, I get one
of those things,

01:24.516 --> 01:26.301
it's gonna be a buffet
of beave.

01:26.368 --> 01:28.237
Mmm, I don't know.
Seems stupid to me.

01:31.510 --> 01:33.679
Thanks to all of you for coming
out today.

01:33.746 --> 01:35.114
In just a minute, we'll begin

01:35.182 --> 01:37.351
our "Hands On A Hard Body"
contest.

01:37.419 --> 01:40.539
And the lucky one of you who can
keep his or her hand on

01:40.606 --> 01:42.675
this dirt bike for the longest
amount of time

01:42.743 --> 01:44.511
will get to take it home!

01:44.596 --> 01:46.731
(all cheer)
Yeah, all right! Yeah!

01:46.799 --> 01:49.603
Okay, everyone who wants to win
this dirt bike,

01:49.670 --> 01:52.073
come on up and put a hand on it!

01:55.613 --> 01:57.665
Mr. Pewterschmidt?
What are you doin' here?

01:57.732 --> 01:59.367
You want
a used dirt bike?

01:59.452 --> 02:02.255
Oh, not at all. But Lois told
me how much you wanted it.

02:02.322 --> 02:03.724
So I decided to win it
for myself

02:03.791 --> 02:05.510
just so I could destroy
it in front of you.

02:05.578 --> 02:07.479
And the clock starts...

02:07.547 --> 02:08.814
now!

02:08.882 --> 02:10.300
How are you gonna destroy
a dirt bike?

02:10.368 --> 02:11.702
You can't even open
your own aspirin.

02:11.770 --> 02:12.603
With that.

02:14.607 --> 02:16.292
Aw, damn it!

02:16.360 --> 02:19.798
Ooh! Our first hand off
the dirt bike!

02:19.865 --> 02:21.884
Huh. I guess you're out,
Mr. Pewterschmidt.

02:21.952 --> 02:23.587
Well, I already paid
for that thing.

02:23.655 --> 02:25.239
So I'm just
gonna stick around

02:25.306 --> 02:26.658
and smash other
stuff you like.

02:28.628 --> 02:31.064
Hey, fatass, you like, um...

02:31.132 --> 02:32.416
you like, uh...

02:32.484 --> 02:33.619
this-this bus bench?

02:33.686 --> 02:35.722
Uh, I, it's okay.

02:35.789 --> 02:38.192
All right, that's good enough
for me. I'm smashing it!

03:59.597 --> 04:02.301
Ha-ha! You loved that thing.

04:09.612 --> 04:11.681
♪ ♪

04:21.313 --> 04:22.581
Amazing!

04:22.649 --> 04:24.117
Nine hours with no break!

04:24.185 --> 04:26.237
Who's gonna win this thing?

04:26.305 --> 04:28.240
You might as well give up now,
Mr. Mayor.

04:28.308 --> 04:29.475
This dirt bike is mine.

04:29.542 --> 04:30.927
Like heck, it is!

04:30.995 --> 04:32.061
(dialing tones)

04:32.130 --> 04:33.431
Hey, check your phone.

04:33.498 --> 04:34.900
Why?

04:34.967 --> 04:37.303
I just sent you a picture
of a kitten in sunglasses.

04:37.371 --> 04:39.039
Well, this I gotta see!

04:39.107 --> 04:41.075
Hello, cool kitty.

04:41.143 --> 04:42.110
Oh...!

04:42.179 --> 04:44.314
And we have a winner!

04:44.398 --> 04:46.317
(cheering)

04:46.385 --> 04:47.819
Aw, darn it.

04:47.886 --> 04:49.822
Well, I guess
I'll just disappear

04:49.889 --> 04:52.226
into that field of corn.

04:55.465 --> 04:58.969
Help! I'm lost in corn!

05:02.359 --> 05:04.126
Hey, where's Peter?

05:04.194 --> 05:07.482
I don't know. I haven't heard
from him since he left work.

05:07.566 --> 05:09.835
Hope you made extra.
I brought a guest.

05:09.903 --> 05:11.704
What the hell?! Who is this?!

05:11.772 --> 05:13.574
This is my dirt bike girlfriend.

05:13.642 --> 05:14.609
Amber.

05:14.677 --> 05:16.044
I'm a dirt bike guy now,

05:16.112 --> 05:17.346
so I need a dirt bike
girlfriend.

05:17.414 --> 05:18.549
Yes, she has small breasts,

05:18.616 --> 05:20.150
but she makes up
for it by smoking.

05:20.218 --> 05:21.219
Peter, she has to leave.

05:21.287 --> 05:22.621
We're havin' dinner.

05:22.689 --> 05:25.192
No, Lois! I will not allow you
to look down on Amber

05:25.259 --> 05:27.461
just 'cause she goes to an
alternative high school!

05:27.529 --> 05:29.631
There's different ways
to measure intelligence

05:29.699 --> 05:31.167
besides someone's
grade-point average!

05:31.235 --> 05:33.237
Fact is, she rumpled up some
poetry she wrote

05:33.305 --> 05:35.040
and threw it away in a fit,

05:35.107 --> 05:37.376
but I unrumpled it,
and it was really good!

05:37.444 --> 05:39.580
(sighs) Fine.
Amber, would you like to have

05:39.647 --> 05:41.082
some dinner with our family?

05:41.150 --> 05:42.383
Nah, I can't.

05:42.451 --> 05:45.088
I got a wicked bruise on
the back of my throat.

05:45.156 --> 05:48.527
ANNOUNCER: Ladies and gentlemen,
please rise for our national anthem,

05:48.595 --> 05:52.733
performed this afternoon by
Peter Griffin and his dirt bike.

05:55.004 --> 05:58.541
(engine revs to the tune
of "The Star-Spangled Banner")

06:17.804 --> 06:18.872
There it is, Meg.

06:18.940 --> 06:20.959
What do you say
we take it for a spin?

06:21.026 --> 06:22.026
Chris, get off there.

06:22.094 --> 06:23.596
You shouldn't
be sitting on that.

06:23.663 --> 06:24.630
Come on.

06:24.698 --> 06:27.184
(clucking)

06:30.740 --> 06:31.975
That's fake.

06:32.042 --> 06:34.278
Come on, Meg, just get on!

06:34.346 --> 06:35.930
(sighs)

06:45.796 --> 06:47.548
Hey, Meg, check it out.

06:47.615 --> 06:49.668
I'm gonna jump
that fire hydrant.

06:49.752 --> 06:52.088
Chris, don't!
You're gonna wreck Dad's bike!

06:52.139 --> 06:54.642
Too late, I already
narrowed my eyes.

07:00.234 --> 07:01.819
(Meg screams)

07:03.323 --> 07:05.492
Chris, you idiot!
Look at what you did!

07:05.559 --> 07:07.945
You mean look what two black
teenagers did

07:07.996 --> 07:09.665
when they stole Dad's bike.

07:12.936 --> 07:14.571
What were you
kids thinking?!

07:14.639 --> 07:15.974
You could have
been killed!

07:16.042 --> 07:18.244
It was Chris' idea.
He talked me into it.

07:18.311 --> 07:19.546
Is that right?

07:19.614 --> 07:21.048
So you like taking
dirt bikes

07:21.116 --> 07:22.583
that don't belong
to you, huh?

07:22.651 --> 07:24.536
Then here, have a whole
carton of cigarettes!

07:24.604 --> 07:25.739
W-what?!

07:25.806 --> 07:27.358
Peter, that's not what
this is about.

07:27.426 --> 07:28.726
See how you like 'em!

07:28.794 --> 07:30.362
Here, I'll even
get you started.

07:30.430 --> 07:31.981
(coughs)

07:32.049 --> 07:33.217
Dad, I don't smoke.

07:33.284 --> 07:34.985
Sure, you don't now.
But keep at it.

07:35.053 --> 07:35.987
You'll get the hang of it.

07:36.055 --> 07:37.673
By the end of that pack,

07:37.741 --> 07:40.093
you'll be smoking like a real pro.
Like a cool kid.

07:40.161 --> 07:41.245
There, that's it.

07:41.313 --> 07:42.213
Gettin' smoother,
isn't it?

07:42.281 --> 07:43.549
Yeah.
Oh, yeah!

07:43.633 --> 07:45.835
Wait till you try it
after a meal. Delicious!

07:45.903 --> 07:47.555
And after sex?
Forget about it.

07:47.622 --> 07:50.025
It's like puttin' your penis
to sleep in a feather bed.

07:50.093 --> 07:51.811
I think I may want
more cigarettes.

07:51.879 --> 07:53.096
Oh, I'll get you more
cigarettes.

07:53.163 --> 07:54.698
But I'm pretty mad
about my dirt bike!

07:54.766 --> 07:56.101
Kids, I'm sorry to say this,

07:56.168 --> 07:58.504
but I think the two of you need
to be punished.

07:58.572 --> 07:59.940
Look, it was
an accident, okay?

08:00.007 --> 08:02.243
I mean, you can always buy
another one, right?

08:02.311 --> 08:03.545
Buy another one?!

08:03.613 --> 08:05.381
You know, I don't think
you kids appreciate

08:05.449 --> 08:06.783
how hard your father
and I work

08:06.851 --> 08:08.319
to provide you with
everything we do.

08:08.386 --> 08:11.289
Sometimes you just seem
to take us for granted.

08:11.358 --> 08:13.326
You know, it's very
difficult bein' a parent.

08:13.394 --> 08:14.762
No, it's not.

08:14.829 --> 08:16.364
You get to do
anything you want.

08:16.432 --> 08:18.100
And you get to make
all the rules.

08:18.168 --> 08:20.537
Damn right I do,
'cause I make the money!

08:20.605 --> 08:23.007
I'm the big...
mamoo around here!

08:23.075 --> 08:24.910
Now, w-w-when you start bringin'
in a paycheck

08:24.978 --> 08:27.347
and providin' for this family,
then you can make the rules!

08:27.414 --> 08:29.450
Well, I'd do a better
job of it than you!

08:29.519 --> 08:31.086
Oh, you think so, huh?

08:31.154 --> 08:33.590
Well, maybe you'd like
to try it for a little while.

08:33.658 --> 08:34.691
You be the adults!

08:34.759 --> 08:35.960
What do you mean?

08:36.028 --> 08:38.430
I mean, maybe we try
a little experiment.

08:38.498 --> 08:40.867
You kids switch places
with your dad and me.

08:40.935 --> 08:44.673
For the next week, you'll be the
parents and we'll be the kids.

08:44.741 --> 08:46.242
Seriously?
Yeah, that'd be awesome!

08:46.310 --> 08:47.410
That sounds great!

08:47.478 --> 08:49.648
That's a great idea, Lois.
Crisscross!

08:49.715 --> 08:51.383
Yes, that is
a crisscross.

08:51.450 --> 08:52.418
Yes!

08:52.486 --> 08:53.620
So we got a deal?

08:53.688 --> 08:54.855
Yeah, we got a deal.

08:54.923 --> 08:56.257
Face-off!

08:56.325 --> 08:57.525
No, Peter.

08:57.593 --> 08:58.561
<i>Road House.</i>

09:05.161 --> 09:06.862
Here's your breakfast, Lois.

09:06.930 --> 09:08.699
Thank you, Mom.

09:08.766 --> 09:10.935
Wh-wh-what is,
what is this?

09:11.003 --> 09:12.504
What's goin' on?

09:12.572 --> 09:14.291
Oh, apparently, Chris and
Meg are switching places

09:14.358 --> 09:16.327
with Peter and Lois
for the week.

09:16.395 --> 09:17.495
Myah!

09:17.562 --> 09:19.731
Hey, Mom, do you mind
if I go shoppin'

09:19.800 --> 09:21.034
with Jennifer
after school?

09:21.101 --> 09:22.836
No, Peter, no, no,
you're still you.

09:22.904 --> 09:24.606
Y-you're just a teenager.

09:24.674 --> 09:25.740
You're not
switching genders.

09:25.809 --> 09:28.011
Ah. I shall return.

09:30.215 --> 09:32.534
Well, I'm off to work
at the brewery.

09:32.602 --> 09:34.471
Okay, have
a good day, honey.

09:34.538 --> 09:36.674
You know, Brian, you
and I should do... No.

09:36.742 --> 09:39.394
Okay, it just,
it-it-it... it looked fun.

09:39.479 --> 09:42.883
All right, time to make
all those popular kids pay

09:42.951 --> 09:44.452
for ignoring me!

09:44.520 --> 09:47.390
Peter, no, y-you're just
a normal high school kid.

09:47.457 --> 09:50.111
Oh.

09:50.179 --> 09:51.596
Hey, Lance,
it's off, it's off.

09:51.664 --> 09:53.365
It's off, it's off.

09:53.433 --> 09:54.718
(gunfire, screams over phone)

09:54.785 --> 09:56.253
Throw this phone
away, Lois!

09:59.192 --> 10:02.229
Griffin, did you finish
those reports I gave you?

10:02.297 --> 10:03.864
Right here, Angela.

10:03.932 --> 10:07.203
Wow. You know, I gotta say,
when your dad told me

10:07.270 --> 10:08.939
about this whole switching
places thing,

10:09.007 --> 10:10.541
I was kinda skeptical,

10:10.609 --> 10:12.778
but you're actually
doing good work.

10:12.846 --> 10:14.848
Well, it's a lot easier
than high school,

10:14.915 --> 10:16.032
I'll tell you that.

10:16.101 --> 10:17.351
Well, how do you mean?

10:17.419 --> 10:18.954
<i>High school's like
Lord of the Flies.</i>

10:19.022 --> 10:20.490
It's a social nightmare.

10:20.557 --> 10:23.260
And I-I hear Canadian high
schools are even worse.

10:23.328 --> 10:27.266
Well, well, look who
matriculated to grade nine.

10:27.334 --> 10:29.569
Someone wants
to get into university.

10:29.637 --> 10:31.606
Hey, guys, I'm sorry.

10:31.673 --> 10:32.941
Well, you're gonna be "sore-y"

10:33.009 --> 10:35.045
when we put you in
the hospital for free, eh?

10:36.865 --> 10:40.369
(cheering)

10:40.437 --> 10:42.272
I don't know what the kids are
complainin' about.

10:42.340 --> 10:43.240
This ain't so bad.

10:43.308 --> 10:44.743
I know, this is fun.

10:44.810 --> 10:46.712
I haven't been
to a pep rally in years.

10:46.780 --> 10:48.298
Do you have school spirit?!

10:48.382 --> 10:49.549
Yeah!

10:49.617 --> 10:51.552
Do you have school spirit?!

10:51.620 --> 10:52.755
Yeah!

10:52.806 --> 10:54.724
Who's got
the most school spirit?!

10:54.792 --> 10:55.825
I do!

10:55.893 --> 10:58.780
Show me
your school spirit!

10:58.848 --> 11:00.065
(inhales)

11:03.738 --> 11:06.207
The players will remember
this while they're playing.

11:09.147 --> 11:10.481
Hey, Mom, where
the hell's dinner?

11:10.549 --> 11:11.549
I'm starving.

11:11.617 --> 11:13.786
Oh man, can you
imagine the disaster

11:13.853 --> 11:15.188
she's gonna
walk out here with?

11:15.256 --> 11:17.758
She has no idea how
hard it is to cook.

11:17.826 --> 11:20.395
Yeah, yeah, I bet-- I bet
she comes out with just like--

11:20.464 --> 11:22.031
just like a poop
on a plate, right?

11:22.099 --> 11:24.101
Poop on a plate would be
good, because at least

11:24.169 --> 11:26.154
there'd be traces
of my food still in there.

11:26.222 --> 11:28.525
Oh ho ho, snap! Snap! Snap!

11:28.593 --> 11:29.726
Hey, guys?

11:29.794 --> 11:31.329
Give her a (bleep)
chance, all right?

11:31.396 --> 11:33.132
Here it is, gang.

11:33.199 --> 11:36.904
Seared ahi tostadas,
grilled asparagus, couscous,

11:36.972 --> 11:39.875
and for dessert, molten
chocolate lava cake.

11:41.945 --> 11:44.164
Wait a minute.

11:44.232 --> 11:46.702
Meg, when did you find
the time to do all this?

11:46.770 --> 11:48.437
Oh, I had all day to do this.

11:48.505 --> 11:49.873
Mm.

11:49.941 --> 11:51.809
Oh my God, this is delicious.

11:51.877 --> 11:53.745
Wh-- what do you
mean "all day"?

11:53.813 --> 11:55.315
W-What about all
the housework?

11:55.382 --> 11:57.818
I did it in like an hour.
I don't understand why

11:57.886 --> 11:59.621
you're such a freakin'
martyr all the time.

11:59.689 --> 12:00.655
It's a house.

12:00.724 --> 12:02.141
It's a finite area.

12:02.209 --> 12:03.694
I'm not cleaning a town.

12:03.745 --> 12:05.980
Hey, family, I'm home.

12:06.048 --> 12:08.217
Ooh, that smells fantastic.

12:08.285 --> 12:10.888
Hey, buddy, how was your first
day in the real world?

12:10.956 --> 12:12.557
It was actually really great.

12:12.624 --> 12:14.961
And Angela even told me
I might get a raise

12:15.029 --> 12:16.462
for doing such a good job.

12:16.530 --> 12:18.449
Wow, guys, you hear that?

12:18.516 --> 12:19.501
A raise.

12:19.569 --> 12:20.769
Hm, interesting.

12:20.837 --> 12:22.672
Seems like the kids are
doing pretty well

12:22.739 --> 12:24.007
at this grown-up thing, huh?

12:24.075 --> 12:26.177
I would suggest
that you suck that.

12:26.245 --> 12:28.647
Wow, I am already
so stuffed.

12:28.715 --> 12:30.183
Guess I shouldn't have had

12:30.251 --> 12:31.819
so many action figure
guns for lunch.

12:38.513 --> 12:40.365
Well, hello, you two.

12:40.433 --> 12:42.001
How's your little
experiment going?

12:42.069 --> 12:43.737
(sobbing):
Horrible.

12:43.805 --> 12:47.009
Three girls I don't care about
made me cry in the bathroom.

12:49.013 --> 12:51.165
Um, hey, you guys.

12:51.233 --> 12:54.353
I bet you Lois Griffin
doesn't make the track team,

12:54.437 --> 12:56.673
which is an important thing
in high school right now.

12:56.740 --> 12:58.259
Yeah, everyone who's
anyone is running track

12:58.326 --> 12:59.945
at our high school right now.

12:59.996 --> 13:02.748
Yeah, and I bet she also doesn't
live on the south side of town,

13:02.816 --> 13:04.201
which is suddenly important.

13:04.269 --> 13:06.337
(all laughing)

13:08.041 --> 13:09.342
(sobbing)

13:09.410 --> 13:12.330
I hate your north side face.

13:12.397 --> 13:14.333
Lois, that's terrible.

13:14.400 --> 13:15.885
My day was even worse.

13:15.953 --> 13:17.788
I got pegged by a
new form of spitball.

13:21.060 --> 13:21.894
(mooing)

13:26.635 --> 13:28.304
(gasping)

13:28.371 --> 13:29.639
Hey, get up,
you faker.

13:29.707 --> 13:31.107
It's just
a spitball.

13:32.978 --> 13:35.832
Hi, family, I'm home.

13:35.899 --> 13:37.568
Oh, Chris,
there you are.

13:37.635 --> 13:39.270
Good, now that
you're both here,

13:39.338 --> 13:41.106
your father and I have
something to say.

13:41.173 --> 13:43.343
Kids, we're callin' off
the experiment early.

13:43.411 --> 13:44.828
What? Why?

13:44.896 --> 13:46.314
Because you were right.

13:46.382 --> 13:48.751
Being a kid is a lot harder
than bein' an adult.

13:48.818 --> 13:51.037
High school sucks.
Everything sucks.

13:51.105 --> 13:53.174
So let's just put things
back the way they were

13:53.241 --> 13:54.860
and just forget all about
this, all right?

13:54.927 --> 13:57.564
You kids go back to school,
Lois goes back to groceries,

13:57.632 --> 13:58.849
I go back to my job.

13:58.917 --> 14:00.185
That's not gonna
work out, Dad.

14:00.252 --> 14:01.387
Why not?

14:01.455 --> 14:03.122
'Cause you don't have
a job anymore.

14:03.190 --> 14:04.958
What? Chris, what do you mean?

14:05.026 --> 14:07.463
Angela fired you
and hired me.

14:07.530 --> 14:10.133
She said I've been doing twice
as good a job as you did.

14:10.201 --> 14:13.187
So from now on, I'm the
breadwinner in this house.

14:13.255 --> 14:15.491
Hey, I forget. Were you
in for this or not?

14:22.399 --> 14:24.468
Chris, you are not
taking Peter's job.

14:24.554 --> 14:26.889
You're a 14-year-old boy,
and you belong in school.

14:26.957 --> 14:29.226
Why, so I can get
a job someday?

14:29.294 --> 14:30.628
I already have a job.

14:30.696 --> 14:32.982
Chris, we're not gonna
allow you to do this.

14:33.049 --> 14:34.785
I seem to remember
somebody saying

14:34.852 --> 14:37.038
the breadwinner
makes the rules.

14:37.105 --> 14:39.826
Well, I'm the breadwinner.
And you know what?

14:39.894 --> 14:42.429
I like being a grown-up,
and I wanna stay this way.

14:42.497 --> 14:44.099
Well, Lois, practically
speaking,

14:44.167 --> 14:46.068
somebody's gotta pay
the bills around here.

14:46.136 --> 14:47.888
Seems like you don't
have a choice

14:47.956 --> 14:49.556
but to let Chris work
at the brewery

14:49.624 --> 14:50.992
until Peter finds a new job.

14:51.060 --> 14:52.728
Well, I suppose that
makes sense.

14:52.796 --> 14:55.298
I guess it could take
Peter a long time

14:55.366 --> 14:56.834
to find a job
in this economy.

14:56.902 --> 14:58.570
Well, it may not
be that bad, Lois.

14:58.638 --> 15:00.440
I could see about
getting back my old job

15:00.508 --> 15:01.942
as a police sketch artist.

15:02.010 --> 15:04.312
Now, did you get a look
at the man who assaulted you?

15:04.380 --> 15:06.182
I did.
Okay, can I get a description?

15:06.250 --> 15:08.652
Yeah, he was probably
around five-nine, five-ten?

15:08.720 --> 15:09.954
Which is it, five-nine
or five-ten?

15:10.022 --> 15:11.456
I'd say five-ten.

15:11.507 --> 15:12.858
Okay, we'll go
five-nine and a half.

15:12.926 --> 15:14.060
And now, how old was he?

15:14.128 --> 15:15.997
Late 30's, maybe 37.

15:16.064 --> 15:17.765
I-I don't know, anywhere
between 35 and 40.

15:17.833 --> 15:19.234
Okay, well, let's say 37.

15:19.302 --> 15:20.303
How about ethnicity?

15:20.371 --> 15:21.638
Yeah, he was Asian-American.

15:21.705 --> 15:22.940
Asian-American.

15:23.008 --> 15:24.492
Are we talking Korean?
Are we talking Thai?

15:24.560 --> 15:25.510
Are we talking Vietnamese?

15:25.578 --> 15:26.779
Maybe Korean.

15:26.847 --> 15:29.299
Could have been Japanese,
but I-I think Korean.

15:29.367 --> 15:30.752
Okay, Korean.

15:30.819 --> 15:32.104
Now how about identifying
characteristics?

15:32.172 --> 15:33.572
Any-any marks, piercings?

15:33.640 --> 15:36.244
He may have had a tattoo.
He may have had a tattoo?

15:36.311 --> 15:37.562
Did have a tattoo?
Which one was it?

15:37.629 --> 15:39.631
I-I don't know, it-- it
all happened so fast.

15:39.699 --> 15:40.867
You know what?
It's fine.

15:40.935 --> 15:42.052
I have a preliminary
sketch here.

15:42.137 --> 15:43.637
Is this the man
who assaulted you?

15:43.705 --> 15:45.874
Peter, they're never
gonna take you back.

15:45.942 --> 15:47.910
You got fired for
racist drawings.

15:47.978 --> 15:49.329
I guess.

15:49.397 --> 15:51.432
Hey, you know what else
I draw really well? Bullwinkle.

15:51.517 --> 15:52.735
I'd probably still be working

15:52.802 --> 15:54.070
if more crooks
looked like Bullwinkle.

15:59.228 --> 16:00.697
Early night, Griffin?

16:00.764 --> 16:02.800
Well, actually, it's 8:00.

16:02.867 --> 16:05.170
Well, did you finish
all the accounts payable

16:05.237 --> 16:06.405
and the accounts receivable?

16:06.473 --> 16:08.007
But that's not my department.

16:08.075 --> 16:09.676
It is now.

16:09.744 --> 16:11.179
The company's making
cutbacks.

16:11.246 --> 16:14.250
You can handle it, it's just
a little extra paperwork.

16:19.859 --> 16:21.611
♪ ♪

16:36.050 --> 16:38.887
Ugh. I am exhausted.

16:51.173 --> 16:54.059
Can this day get
any more stressful?

17:00.236 --> 17:04.174
"Wanted: Muscular man for
discreet pushing and pulling."

17:04.242 --> 17:05.927
Well, I'm not above
manual labor.

17:05.995 --> 17:08.598
Oh, hi, Chris.
How was your day?

17:08.666 --> 17:10.651
You know what
would be great?

17:10.719 --> 17:13.138
If I could come home
and have five minutes

17:13.206 --> 17:15.175
before you jump
all over my back.

17:15.242 --> 17:16.944
Also, she broke a plate.

17:17.012 --> 17:19.448
And what about you?
Did you get a job today?

17:19.515 --> 17:21.984
(chuckles)
I kind of got one.

17:22.052 --> 17:23.921
Right, Lois? Right?

17:23.988 --> 17:25.557
So, Chris, good day
at the office?

17:25.624 --> 17:27.943
You know, actually, Angela
said that the spreadsheets

17:28.011 --> 17:30.347
I presented were beyond the
projections for last quarter.

17:30.415 --> 17:31.749
Oh, is that good?

17:31.817 --> 17:33.469
You know what?! Never mind!

17:35.256 --> 17:36.974
Now I'm mad at you!

17:40.981 --> 17:43.216
Peter, I'm really
worried about Chris.

17:43.268 --> 17:45.637
All this pressure seems
to be getting to him.

17:45.704 --> 17:47.173
I know, he's turning
into a jerk.

17:48.408 --> 17:50.177
Oh, hey, Chris.

17:50.244 --> 17:51.846
You wanna keep it down in here?

17:51.914 --> 17:54.016
One of us has to work
in the morning.

17:54.084 --> 17:56.152
Chris, have you--
have you been drinking?

17:56.220 --> 17:58.957
Yes. Have you been aging?

17:59.025 --> 18:01.694
I want you two to do it
right in front of me.

18:01.762 --> 18:03.964
And I'm gonna throw 40 bucks
on your sweaty bodies

18:04.032 --> 18:05.800
when you're done.

18:05.868 --> 18:07.186
Let's see the money.

18:07.253 --> 18:09.823
Why do you guys hate me?

18:09.891 --> 18:13.362
Ugh, that pain in my
stomach is back.

18:13.429 --> 18:18.636
Ow!

18:20.089 --> 18:22.391
What? What?

18:22.459 --> 18:23.927
What are you looking at?

18:23.995 --> 18:25.797
I could fight you both.

18:25.865 --> 18:28.717
You don't know what
I go through every day.

18:28.785 --> 18:30.153
(sobbing)

18:30.221 --> 18:34.343
Now go to sleep,
the both of you.

18:34.410 --> 18:37.081
PETER (whimpering): I think we
should go live with Mom.

18:37.149 --> 18:38.716
STEWIE:
I just heard all of that,

18:38.783 --> 18:41.420
and I just wanna say this family
is (bleep) disintegrating.

18:47.164 --> 18:48.631
Oh, hey, Chris, by the way,

18:48.698 --> 18:50.066
the roofer came today
while you were at work.

18:50.134 --> 18:51.151
And?

18:51.203 --> 18:52.653
It's gonna be
five grand to fix it.

18:52.721 --> 18:54.756
Oh that's just perfect.

18:54.824 --> 18:57.828
I love spending $5,000 on
something nobody can see.

18:57.896 --> 18:59.548
Anyone got more happy news?

18:59.615 --> 19:01.517
I'm gonna need
a check for the dentist.

19:01.585 --> 19:03.019
Peter has two cavities.

19:03.086 --> 19:05.456
I'll bet if I go upstairs
to that bathroom

19:05.524 --> 19:07.326
that toothbrush is
as dry as a bone.

19:07.394 --> 19:09.128
Sometimes I forget.

19:09.197 --> 19:11.349
Anything else I should
know about?!

19:11.416 --> 19:14.019
Well, my science class
is taking a field trip

19:14.087 --> 19:15.622
to the water
purification center.

19:15.689 --> 19:19.059
And? And it costs ten dollars
for lunch and the bus.

19:19.127 --> 19:20.662
Ten dollars?

19:20.730 --> 19:22.815
What-- What the hell is
it with that school

19:22.883 --> 19:25.185
that every time you walk in there
somebody wants ten dollars?!

19:25.253 --> 19:27.105
Look, I-I'm really sorry,

19:27.172 --> 19:28.524
but if we're that
desperate for money,

19:28.592 --> 19:30.010
isn't there something we can do?

19:30.061 --> 19:31.896
I mean, maybe we could ask

19:31.964 --> 19:33.365
to borrow some
from Mr. Quagmire.

19:33.433 --> 19:35.167
Oh, you'd like that,
wouldn't you?

19:35.235 --> 19:36.970
Like to see me
walk next door,

19:37.037 --> 19:38.772
hat in hand, and
ask him for money.

19:38.840 --> 19:40.742
Bet you'd have your nose
pressed against the glass

19:40.810 --> 19:42.745
to watch that conversation.

19:42.813 --> 19:44.715
No, you know what? Instead, let's
just go knock on all the doors

19:44.782 --> 19:46.584
of all our neighbors and
tell 'em I'm a failure!

19:46.652 --> 19:49.439
No, that's not what I...
No, no, no, it's a good idea.

19:49.507 --> 19:52.076
Let's just go right now and tell
everyone how much of a failure I am.

19:52.144 --> 19:53.010
But I...

19:54.981 --> 19:57.751
(knocking)
QUAGMIRE:
Oh, hey, Chris.

19:57.819 --> 19:59.938
CHRIS: Meg has something
she wants to tell you.

20:00.006 --> 20:02.458
Chris, please, I'm sorry.
CHRIS: Say it!

20:02.526 --> 20:03.910
MEG (crying):
Chris is a failure.

20:03.978 --> 20:05.445
QUAGMIRE:
Uh, okay.

20:05.514 --> 20:07.315
CHRIS: Now we're going
to the Swansons!

20:07.399 --> 20:09.101
(Meg sobbing)

20:09.169 --> 20:11.421
(Chris grunting)

20:11.489 --> 20:13.825
(yelling)

20:13.910 --> 20:15.110
Oh, my God!

20:15.161 --> 20:16.996
I think Chris is
having a heart attack!

20:17.081 --> 20:18.832
We're not aspose'ta
leave the table.

20:24.058 --> 20:26.127
Be cool, be quiet, be quiet.

20:28.515 --> 20:30.033
All right, well,
nothing to worry about.

20:30.101 --> 20:31.384
Chris is going to
be just fine.

20:34.090 --> 20:37.010
Oh, Chris, I'm so
glad you're okay.

20:37.077 --> 20:38.512
What-- what happened?

20:38.580 --> 20:40.465
You had a
heart attack, sweetie.

20:40.533 --> 20:41.967
A heart attack?

20:42.035 --> 20:44.320
Yeah, you almost worked yourself
right into the ground, buddy.

20:44.372 --> 20:46.841
Oh, it's all our fault.
We never should have let you

20:46.909 --> 20:48.444
take on the pressure
of being an adult.

20:48.511 --> 20:50.113
It's okay, Mom.

20:50.181 --> 20:51.849
Boy, I thought being a grown-up

20:51.917 --> 20:53.317
would be easier
than being a kid.

20:53.385 --> 20:55.287
But it turned out
it was just as hard.

20:55.355 --> 20:58.125
I guess what we all learned is
that no matter who you are,

20:58.193 --> 21:00.995
or where you come from,
life is a terrible thing.

21:01.063 --> 21:03.900
Yeah, but if you got your family
to help you get through it,

21:03.968 --> 21:05.168
it's not quite as bad.

21:05.236 --> 21:07.405
And, hey, at least
I get my old job back.

21:07.473 --> 21:09.876
You know, from now on,
let's not complain so much.

21:14.901 --> 21:16.903
Hey, what do you guys do
after the screen goes black?

21:16.904 --> 22:17.904
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru